      "Explanation": "A Brahmin wanderer is a social label, not one biography. Chan collections use it for distinct case figures: Long-Claw argues that he accepts nothing, while the Black-clan Brahmin is ordered by Shakyamuni to put down what remains after both flowers are released. Fengxue Yanzhao also raises Hanshan’s verse about a Brahmin dying and meeting Yama. The entry therefore keeps the category separate from any one named wanderer."
